WEBVTT

00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:04.845
After a jaw is cut in surgery, the pieces must stay still while the bone heals.

00:00:05.645 --> 00:00:10.275
The surgeon lines up the pieces. Then they bend a thin titanium plate to fit the bone.

00:00:11.075 --> 00:00:13.417
A drill makes a hole straight through the plate,

00:00:13.417 --> 00:00:14.979
with cool water running over it.

00:00:15.779 --> 00:00:18.744
Short screws hold the plate, two on each side of the cut.

00:00:19.544 --> 00:00:21.941
They go only into the hard outer layer of bone,

00:00:21.941 --> 00:00:23.981
away from the tooth roots and the nerve.
